 - Writes require the `contributor` or `manager` role in the project. Users who can read but not write get 403.
 - Contributors may only modify tasks assigned to themselves, and may not reassign tasks. Managers may modify any task.
 - Only managers may delete tasks.
+- Moving a task requires the manager role in both the source and the destination project. The destination must exist and be readable (else 404), and must not be archived (else 409). The task keeps its ID, title, status and assignee; if it has an assignee, that user must be a contributor or manager of the destination, otherwise the move is rejected with 400.
 - Archived projects reject all writes with 409 (reads still work).
